{
  "name": "How to Get Ready for a Handyman Visit",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting ready for a handyman to tackle those nagging household repairs doesn’t have to be a big ordeal, but a little preparation can make things go super smoothly. First, describe the problem clearly. The more details you can give, the better they can prepare! Think about what’s happening, when it started, and any symptoms you've noticed. Next, confirm whether the task is something they typically handle. Most handymen, like HH Remodeling LLC, cover things like drywall patching, fixing leaky faucets, or installing new fixtures. Once you’re on the same page about the scope, get a clear time and cost estimate. This helps set expectations and avoids any surprises down the road. You’ll also want to verify whether materials and tools are included in the estimate or if you need to provide anything. Finally, schedule a repair window that works for you. While many common repairs are quick jobs, clarifying the expected completion time in advance is always a good idea, as it can vary with complexity. Being prepared helps ensure your repair is done efficiently and to your satisfaction. Give us a call at HH Remodeling LLC if you have any questions!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
